{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.641,
   "text": "The week I moved to Alder Falls, my neighbor told me the town's only rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.241,
   "end": 15.471,
   "text": "If the clock in the square ever strikes thirteen... turn off every light, and stay away from the windows."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.171,
   "end": 18.155,
   "text": "I laughed. She didn't."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 19.255,
   "end": 23.116,
   "text": "Two months later, the bells woke me just after midnight."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 23.716,
   "end": 26.959,
   "text": "I counted in the dark. Eleven. Twelve."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 27.859,
   "end": 28.904,
   "text": "Thirteen."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 30.904,
   "end": 35.917,
   "text": "Up and down the street, porch lights went out, one by one. All except mine."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 36.617,
   "end": 42.975,
   "text": "Through the gap in the curtains, I saw them. Tall gray shapes, walking slowly down the middle of the road."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 43.575,
   "end": 46.177,
   "text": "Every dark house, they passed."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 46.977,
   "end": 49.239,
   "text": "At mine... they stopped."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 51.839,
   "end": 56.703,
   "text": "I hit the switch so hard it cracked, and I sat on the floor until sunrise."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 57.703,
   "end": 62.097,
   "text": "In the morning, my neighbor was waiting at the fence, pale as paper."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 62.697,
   "end": 67.775,
   "text": "A lit porch is an invitation, she whispered. But you turned it off in time."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 68.975,
   "end": 74.265,
   "text": "Then she looked past me, through my kitchen window... and asked who was making breakfast."
  }
 ],
